  "note": "The list view and /collection rows are photographed BECAUSE they must not change: this round swaps one treatment at one size, and a sweep of only the surfaces that moved cannot show that the small runs stayed discs. The deck rows take PROBE_DECK from the environment — any deck the signed-in account owns. A cost with a hybrid and one with a Phyrexian are separate rows because they are the two symbols the retired disc could not draw at all, and the generic-plus-hue row is the common case they would otherwise hide. The split row is the one surface treatment that differs from every other cost: both halves drawn, separated by the same `//` the printed name carries, where a row draws the front half alone."
